[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ghawken/WeatherFlowTempest/main/Images/banner.png[/img]

[size=150][b]WeatherFlow Tempest Weather Station — Indigo Plugin[/b][/size]

Receives live weather data from [url=https://weatherflow.com/tempest-weather-system/]WeatherFlow Tempest[/url] stations via [b]local UDP broadcast[/b] and maps all sensor observations to Indigo device states. No cloud account is required for basic operation. An optional [b]WeatherFlow Web API[/b] token unlocks authoritative rain totals, rain duration, conditions text, hourly lightning counts, and a [b]web-only mode[/b] that works even when the hub is on a different network.

Wiki: [url=https://github.com/Ghawken/WeatherFlowTempest/wiki]https://github.com/Ghawken/WeatherFlowTempest/wiki[/url]
GitHub: [url=https://github.com/Ghawken/WeatherFlowTempest]https://github.com/Ghawken/WeatherFlowTempest[/url]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ghawken/WeatherFlowTempest/main/Images/weather_divider_top_animated.gif[/img]

[size=125][b]Screenshot[/b][/size]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ghawken/WeatherFlowTempest/main/Images/WeatherFlowStates.png[/img]

[i]Indigo device states for a Tempest Weather Station showing live sensor readings, web-sourced rain totals, and unit labels.[/i]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ghawken/WeatherFlowTempest/main/Images/weather_divider_top_animated.gif[/img]

[size=125][b]Features[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Temperature:[/b] Ambient, feels-like, dew point, wet bulb, wind chill, heat index, delta-T
[*][b]Atmospheric:[/b] Station pressure, sea-level pressure, relative humidity, vapour pressure, air density
[*][b]Wind:[/b] Instantaneous speed/direction (rapid-wind, ~3 s), 1-minute average, gust, lull, cardinal, sample interval
[*][b]Rain:[/b] Per-minute accumulation, rain rate, intensity label, daily total, yesterday's total, Rain Check status
[*][b]Rain (web):[/b] Authoritative rain-check-corrected totals, last-1-hour rain, daily/yesterday rain duration in minutes
[*][b]Lightning:[/b] Strike count, average distance, last-strike distance, energy and timestamp
[*][b]Lightning (web):[/b] Hourly and 3-hour strike counts
[*][b]Conditions (web):[/b] Weather conditions text and icon name from WeatherFlow's forecast engine
[*][b]Light:[/b] Illuminance (lux), solar radiation (W/m²), UV index
[*][b]Battery:[/b] Voltage and percentage; power-save mode label; report interval
[*][b]Derived:[/b] Cloud base, freezing level (both require altitude to be set)
[*][b]Diagnostics:[/b] RSSI, firmware version, sensor fault flags, silence detection
[*][b]Hub:[/b] Firmware, Wi-Fi RSSI, uptime, reset reasons
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ghawken/WeatherFlowTempest/main/Images/weather_divider_top_animated.gif[/img]

[size=125][b]Requirements[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Indigo:[/b] 2025.2 or later (ServerApiVersion 3.4)
[*][b]WeatherFlow hub:[/b] Any — must be on the same subnet as the Indigo Mac, or use web-only mode for remote hubs
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ghawken/WeatherFlowTempest/main/Images/weather_divider_top_animated.gif[/img]

[size=125][b]Quick Start[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Install the plugin (double-click [b]WeatherFlowTempest.indigoPlugin[/b]).
[*]Go to [b]Plugins → WeatherFlow Tempest → Configure → Generate Devices[/b].
[*]Done — states populate within 60 seconds of the first UDP broadcast.
[/list]

See [url=https://github.com/Ghawken/WeatherFlowTempest/wiki/Installation]Installation wiki page[/url] for full details.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ghawken/WeatherFlowTempest/main/Images/weather_divider_top_animated.gif[/img]

[size=125][b]Plugin Configuration[/b][/size]

Open [b]Plugins → WeatherFlow Tempest Weather Station → Configure[/b].

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ghawken/WeatherFlowTempest/main/Images/pluginConfig.png[/img]

[b]Device Generation[/b]

Click [b]Generate Devices[/b] to auto-create Indigo devices for every Tempest and Hub currently broadcasting on the network. Re-press whenever new hardware is added.

[b]UDP Listener Settings[/b]

[list]
[*][b]UDP Port:[/b] Port the hub broadcasts on (default: 50222)
[*][b]Listen Address:[/b] Network interface to listen on (default: 0.0.0.0 = all interfaces)
[/list]

Saving the preferences automatically restarts the UDP listener.

[b]WeatherFlow Web API (Optional)[/b]

[list]
[*][b]Enable Web API:[/b] Tick to activate web-based data polling
[*][b]API Token:[/b] Your Personal Use Token from [url=https://tempestwx.com/settings/tokens]tempestwx.com → Settings → Data Authorizations[/url]
[/list]

When enabled, the plugin polls the WeatherFlow REST API to supplement UDP data with:
[list]
[*][b]Authoritative rain totals[/b] — rain-check corrected daily and yesterday rain
[*][b]Rain last 1 hour[/b] — rolling 1-hour rainfall total
[*][b]Rain duration[/b] — minutes of measurable rain today and yesterday
[*][b]Conditions & icon[/b] — current weather description and icon name
[*][b]Hourly lightning counts[/b] — strikes in the last 1 and 3 hours
[/list]

The web API polls every [b]5 minutes[/b] when UDP data is active, or every [b]60 seconds[/b] in web-only mode.

[quote]Getting a token: Log in to tempestwx.com, go to Settings → Data Authorizations, and generate a Personal Use Token. It is free and tied to your WeatherFlow account.[/quote]

[quote]Note: The WeatherFlow REST API authenticates by account — it only serves stations registered to the token's owner.[/quote]

[b]Debugging Options[/b]

[list]
[*][b]Indigo Log Level:[/b] Verbosity of messages in the Indigo Event Log
[*][b]File Log Level:[/b] Verbosity of messages written to the plugin log file
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ghawken/WeatherFlowTempest/main/Images/weather_divider_top_animated.gif[/img]

[size=125][b]Device Setup[/b][/size]

[b]Auto-create all devices at once (recommended)[/b]

[list=1]
[*]Open [b]Plugins → WeatherFlow Tempest Weather Station → Configure[/b].
[*]Click [b]Generate Devices[/b].
[*]The plugin creates one Indigo device for every Tempest and Hub currently broadcasting on the network.
[*]Re-click the button whenever new hardware is added.
[/list]

[b]Manual device creation[/b]

[list=1]
[*]Go to [b]Devices → New Device → Type: WeatherFlow Tempest Weather Station[/b].
[*]Choose [b]Tempest Weather Station[/b] or [b]WeatherFlow Hub[/b].
[*]Select your unit from the dropdown — devices are listed as soon as the hub broadcasts.
[*]Click [b]Save[/b].
[/list]

[quote]Tip: If the device dropdown is empty, the hub has not yet sent a broadcast. Wait 30–60 seconds and use the Reload button in the dialog to refresh the list.[/quote]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ghawken/WeatherFlowTempest/main/Images/weather_divider_top_animated.gif[/img]

[size=125][b]Tempest Device Configuration[/b][/size]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ghawken/WeatherFlowTempest/main/Images/deviceConfig.png[/img]

[list]
[*][b]Tempest Device:[/b] Serial number of the Tempest (ST-xxxxxxxx), discovered automatically from UDP
[*][b]Web-only (hub on different network):[/b] Tick to bypass UDP and use the web API exclusively — see below
[*][b]Altitude (m):[/b] Station elevation in metres. Used to calculate sea-level pressure, cloud base, and freezing level. Set to 0 to omit those states.
[*][b]Temperature:[/b] °C or °F
[*][b]Pressure:[/b] hPa (mbar), mmHg, or inHg
[*][b]Wind Speed:[/b] m/s, km/h, mph, or knots
[*][b]Rainfall:[/b] mm or inches
[*][b]Altitude unit:[/b] Metres or feet (for cloud base and freezing level)
[/list]

[b]Web-only Mode[/b]

Enable [b]Web-only (hub on different network)[/b] when the Tempest hub is on a separate network from the Indigo Mac (e.g. a remote property or a different VLAN where UDP broadcast doesn't reach).

When web-only is ticked, one additional field appears:
[list]
[*][b]Station ID:[/b] Numeric WeatherFlow station ID — found in the WeatherFlow app under station Settings
[/list]

The Web API must be enabled and a valid token entered in Plugin Preferences. The device is polled every 60 seconds and all states are populated from the web. The [b]deviceStatus[/b] state shows [b]Active (web)[/b] when data is flowing.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ghawken/WeatherFlowTempest/main/Images/weather_divider_top_animated.gif[/img]

[size=125][b]Device States — Tempest Weather Station[/b][/size]

[b]Temperature[/b]
[list]
[*][b]air_temperature[/b] — Ambient temperature
[*][b]temperature[/b] — Alias for air_temperature
[*][b]feels_like_temperature[/b] — Apparent / feels-like temperature
[*][b]dew_point_temperature[/b] — Dew point
[*][b]wet_bulb_temperature[/b] — Wet bulb temperature
[*][b]wind_chill_temperature[/b] — Wind chill
[*][b]heat_index[/b] — Heat index
[*][b]delta_t[/b] — Delta-T (dry bulb minus wet bulb)
[/list]

[b]Atmospheric[/b]
[list]
[*][b]relative_humidity[/b] — Relative humidity (%)
[*][b]station_pressure[/b] — Raw station pressure
[*][b]sea_level_pressure[/b] — Sea-level corrected pressure (requires altitude > 0)
[*][b]vapor_pressure[/b] — Vapour pressure
[*][b]air_density[/b] — Air density (kg/m³, always metric)
[*][b]cloud_base[/b] — Estimated cloud base height (requires altitude > 0)
[*][b]freezing_level[/b] — Estimated freezing level height (requires altitude > 0)
[/list]

[b]Light & UV[/b]
[list]
[*][b]illuminance[/b] — Illuminance (lux)
[*][b]solar_radiation[/b] — Solar irradiance (W/m²)
[*][b]uv[/b] — UV index
[/list]

[b]Rain[/b]
[list]
[*][b]rain_accumulation_previous_minute[/b] — Rain in the previous minute (UDP)
[*][b]rain_rate[/b] — Current rain rate (mm/h or in/h) (UDP)
[*][b]rain_intensity[/b] — None / Very Light / Light / Moderate / Heavy / Violent (UDP)
[*][b]rain_today[/b] — Total rain since local midnight (web value is rain-check corrected)
[*][b]rain_yesterday[/b] — Yesterday's total rain
[*][b]rain_check[/b] — WeatherFlow Rain Check status: none / on / off (UDP)
[*][b]precipitation_type[/b] — none, rain, hail, or rain_hail (UDP)
[*][b]last_rain_start[/b] — Timestamp of the most recent rain-start event (UDP)
[*][b]rain_last_1hr[/b] [color=blue][b](Web API only)[/b][/color] — Rain accumulated in the last 60 minutes
[*][b]rain_duration_today[/b] [color=blue][b](Web API only)[/b][/color] — Minutes of measurable rain today
[*][b]rain_duration_yesterday[/b] [color=blue][b](Web API only)[/b][/color] — Minutes of measurable rain yesterday
[/list]

[b]Lightning[/b]
[list]
[*][b]lightning_strike_count[/b] — Strikes in the last 3 minutes (UDP)
[*][b]lightning_strike_average_distance[/b] — Average distance of recent strikes (UDP)
[*][b]last_strike_distance[/b] — Distance of the most recent strike (UDP)
[*][b]last_strike_energy[/b] — Energy of the most recent strike (UDP)
[*][b]last_strike_time[/b] — Timestamp of the most recent strike (UDP)
[*][b]lightning_count_last_1hr[/b] [color=blue][b](Web API only)[/b][/color] — Strikes in the last 60 minutes
[*][b]lightning_count_last_3hr[/b] [color=blue][b](Web API only)[/b][/color] — Strikes in the last 3 hours
[/list]

[b]Conditions (Web API only)[/b]
[list]
[*][b]conditions[/b] [color=blue][b](Web API only)[/b][/color] — Current weather description (e.g. "Partly Cloudy")
[*][b]weather_icon[/b] [color=blue][b](Web API only)[/b][/color] — Icon name from WeatherFlow's forecast engine
[/list]

[b]Wind[/b]
[list]
[*][b]wind_speed[/b] — Instantaneous wind speed (rapid-wind, ~3 s interval)
[*][b]wind_average[/b] — 1-minute average wind speed
[*][b]wind_gust[/b] — 1-minute wind gust
[*][b]wind_lull[/b] — 1-minute wind lull
[*][b]wind_direction[/b] — Instantaneous wind direction (°)
[*][b]wind_direction_average[/b] — 1-minute average wind direction (°)
[*][b]wind_direction_cardinal[/b] — Instantaneous cardinal direction (N, NE, …)
[*][b]wind_direction_average_cardinal[/b] — Average cardinal direction
[*][b]wind_sample_interval[/b] — Wind measurement window (seconds)
[/list]

[b]Unit Labels[/b]
[list]
[*][b]unit_temperature[/b] — Active temperature unit (e.g. °C)
[*][b]unit_pressure[/b] — Active pressure unit (e.g. hPa)
[*][b]unit_wind[/b] — Active wind speed unit (e.g. km/h)
[*][b]unit_rain[/b] — Active rain unit (e.g. mm)
[/list]

[b]Battery & Power[/b]
[list]
[*][b]battery[/b] — Battery voltage (V)
[*][b]battery_percent[/b] — Battery level (%)
[*][b]power_save_mode[/b] — Active power-save mode name
[*][b]report_interval[/b] — Observation reporting frequency (minutes)
[/list]

[b]Diagnostics[/b]
[list]
[*][b]rssi[/b] — Tempest RF signal strength (dBm)
[*][b]hub_rssi[/b] — Hub RF signal strength (dBm)
[*][b]firmware_revision[/b] — Tempest firmware version
[*][b]hub_sn[/b] — Hub serial number
[*][b]up_since[/b] — Device power-on timestamp (UTC)
[*][b]last_report[/b] — Timestamp of the most recent observation (UTC)
[*][b]sensor_status[/b] — Sensor fault flags, or OK
[*][b]deviceStatus[/b] — Active (UDP) / Active (web) / Waiting for data / No data — last seen N min ago
[/list]

[size=110][b]WeatherFlow Hub[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]firmware_revision[/b] — Hub firmware version
[*][b]rssi[/b] — Hub Wi-Fi signal strength (dBm)
[*][b]up_since[/b] — Hub power-on timestamp (UTC)
[*][b]uptime[/b] — Seconds since last boot
[*][b]reset_flags[/b] — Reason(s) for the last reset (comma-separated)
[*][b]deviceStatus[/b] — Connection status
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ghawken/WeatherFlowTempest/main/Images/weather_divider_top_animated.gif[/img]

[size=125][b]Triggers[/b][/size]

Three custom trigger types are available under [b]Triggers → New Trigger → WeatherFlow Tempest Weather Station[/b].

Each trigger includes a [b]Tempest Device[/b] picker so it can be scoped to a specific station.

[b]Lightning Strike Detected[/b]

Fires whenever the selected Tempest detects a lightning strike. The [b]last_strike_distance[/b], [b]last_strike_energy[/b], and [b]last_strike_time[/b] states are updated before the trigger fires.

[b]Rain Started[/b]

Fires when the Tempest detects the onset of precipitation. Fires once per rain onset — not repeatedly while rain continues. The [b]last_rain_start[/b] state is updated when this trigger fires.

[b]Rapid Wind Exceeds Threshold[/b]

Fires when an instantaneous wind reading meets or exceeds a configurable speed. Readings arrive approximately every [b]3 seconds[/b].

[quote]The threshold is always compared against the raw m/s magnitude regardless of the display unit. 1 m/s = 3.6 km/h = 2.237 mph = 1.944 kn.[/quote]

[b]Trigger Limitations[/b]
[list]
[*]In power-save MODE_2 and above, rapid-wind events are not sent. The [b]wind_speed[/b] state still updates from 1-minute observations.
[*]Lightning and rain-start triggers fire from discrete UDP events and are not affected by power-save mode.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ghawken/WeatherFlowTempest/main/Images/weather_divider_top_animated.gif[/img]

[size=125][b]Station Silence Detection[/b][/size]

If no observation is received for more than [b]5 minutes[/b]:
[list]
[*]The [b]deviceStatus[/b] state is updated to "No data — last seen N min ago".
[*]A warning is written to the Indigo Event Log.
[*]The warning repeats every [b]30 minutes[/b] with an updated elapsed time.
[/list]

When data resumes, [b]deviceStatus[/b] returns to "Active" automatically. The UDP listener and web API poller are both monitored and restarted automatically if they exit unexpectedly.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ghawken/WeatherFlowTempest/main/Images/weather_divider_top_animated.gif[/img]

[size=125][b]Troubleshooting[/b][/size]

[b]Device dropdown is empty / "No devices discovered yet"[/b]
[list]
[*]Confirm the hub is on the same subnet as the Indigo Mac. UDP broadcast does not cross router boundaries.
[*]Check that nothing is blocking UDP port 50222.
[*]Wait 60 seconds, then use the [b]Reload[/b] button in the device dialog.
[*]If the hub is on a different network, use [b]web-only mode[/b] in the device configuration.
[/list]

[b]Web API returns 401 Unauthorized[/b]
[list]
[*]Verify the API token in Plugin Preferences is correct.
[*]Ensure the Station ID in the device config matches a station registered to the token's account.
[*]After 3 consecutive failures, polling is suspended. Correct the station ID and save the device to resume.
[/list]

[b]rain_last_1hr, conditions, weather_icon are empty[/b]
[list]
[*]These states require the Web API to be enabled. Tick [b]Enable Web API[/b] in Plugin Preferences and enter a valid token.
[/list]

[b]sea_level_pressure, cloud_base, freezing_level are missing[/b]
[list]
[*]Set [b]Altitude (m)[/b] to a non-zero value in the Tempest device configuration.
[/list]

[b]sensor_status shows all sensors failed[/b]
[list]
[*]Known firmware quirk (firmware 181). The plugin detects the pattern and shows OK instead. A genuine partial failure shows only the affected sensors.
[/list]

[b]Debug logging[/b]
[list]
[*]Set [b]Indigo Log Level[/b] to Debugging Messages in Plugin Preferences.
[*]Plugin log file: ~/Library/Application Support/Perceptive Automation/Indigo 2025.x/Logs/
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ghawken/WeatherFlowTempest/main/Images/weather_divider_top_animated.gif[/img]

[size=125][b]Libraries & Acknowledgements[/b][/size]

[b][url=https://github.com/natekspencer/pyweatherflowudp]pyweatherflowudp[/url] — v1.5.2[/b]
[i]by Nathan Spencer (@natekspencer)[/i]

The core UDP library. Provides an event-based async interface, parses every WeatherFlow message type, and exposes sensor values as typed properties with full unit support. All derived meteorological calculations are provided by this library.

Licensed under MIT. Consider [url=https://ko-fi.com/natekspencer]supporting Nathan on Ko-fi[/url].

[b][url=https://pint.readthedocs.io/]Pint[/url] — v0.25.3[/b]

Physical quantity handling. All sensor values carry their native unit and are converted to the user's display unit using Pint's unit registry.

[b][url=https://github.com/psychrometrics/psychrolib]PsychroLib[/url] — v2.5.0[/b]

Psychrometric calculations used to derive wet bulb temperature and related humidity metrics.

